yScore":0.017,"scholarlyScore":0.074,"traits":[{"id":"memoiristic","score":0.22,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"confessions\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":18,"criticalRenown":60,"controversy":12,"llmAffinity":82,"affinityResidual":10.32,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.84,"criticalRenown":0.72,"controversy":0.68,"llmAffinity":0.89},"tags":{"craft":"prose-style","evidence":"close-reading","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"primarySubject":"History","secondarySubjects":["Religion","Gender & Sexuality"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book focuses on the historical context of women's experiences in Augustine's Confessions, making 'History' the primary subject, while touching significantly on themes of religion and gender.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"f37b918702e992fdd6c1005a087f8f9617618b53be0606998e1e3d708056ea41","summary":"While many know of Saint Augustine and his Confessions , few are aware of how his life and thought were influenced by women. Queens of a Fallen World tells a story of betrayal, love, and ambition in the ancient world as seen through a woman's eyes. Historian Kate Cooper introduces us to four women whose hopes and plans collided in Augustine's early adulthood: his mother, Monnica of Thagaste; his lover; his fiancée; and Justina, the troubled empress of ancient Rome. Drawing upon their depictions in the Confessions , Cooper skilfully reconstructs their lives against the backdrop of their fourth-century society. Though they came from different walks of life, each found her own way of prevailing in a world ruled by men. A refreshingly complex and compelling portrait of Augustine, Queens of a Fallen World is the riveting story of four remarkable women who set him on course to change history.","displaySummary":"A refreshingly complex and compelling portrait of Augustine, Queens of